[Music]  she eventually got her big bang but she  had to wear a fat suit first and that  was just one step on kaylee cuoco's  journey  kaylee cuoco grew up in camarillo  california which is only an hour away  from los angeles this made kaylie's  early dreams of being a child actor  easier to pursue but her desire to act  came with a deal from her parents she  had to have a back-up plan this led to  kaylee developing many hobbies as a  child aside from acting there was of  course modeling and tennis as a child  but as an adult she has maintained very  eclectic tastes outside of her usual job  including equestrianism and drumming  however it didn't take her long to get  started with her plan a career as she  began landing commercials when she was  about five years old her television  debut came in 1992 when she was cast as  connie reinhardt in the made for tv  movie quicksand no escape from there  cuoco's career was set in motion and she  began landing roles on some of the  decade's most popular shows popping up  in 1994 in episodes of northern exposure  and my so-called life two years later  she was on abc's ellen playing a young  version of ellen degeneres's character  like many child actors kaylie's  increased opportunities eventually led  her to the disney channel throughout her  youth she appeared in numerous disney  productions starting with the tv film  toothless starring kirstie alley as a  dentist turned tooth fairy however one  of her more recognizable roles as a  teenager came with the disney channel  original movie ally cats strike which  was released in 2000 and allowed cuoco  to show off her bowling skills i think  you're doing better soon you learn you'd  have to throw the ball so hard it took  me a long time to learn that  not only was this a big opportunity for  the up-and-coming actor but it ended up  being a pivotal moment in her youth  according to an interview with w  magazine this role led to kaylee's first  kiss though it wasn't on screen she went  on a date with an actor from the movie  who ended up being fired her work with  disney continued from 2004 to 2006 as  she voiced brandy on the animated series  brandy and mr whiskers and lent her  voice talents to the bratz franchise as  kirstie  by the time she was a teenager cuoco was  a nationally ranked tennis player even  though she gave up the sport to pursue  her acting career she decided to  continue her other hobby of riding  horses as she told the new zealand  herald i have six horses and they have  been the biggest blessing in my life  horseback riding is why i'm so centered  especially in this business i wouldn't  have my career without it the next  decade brought even more opportunities  cuoco played maureen mccormick in the tv  movie growing up brady in 2000 that same  year she scored a recurring role on the  cbs sitcom ladies man coming on as  bonnie styles for season two  kaylee cuoco's big break almost didn't  happen thanks to a bad audition however  producers could see she was right for  the show and called her agent asking if  she would try again that's why in 2002  she was cast as bridget on abc's eight  simple rules she played the oldest child  in the hennessey family a beautiful  ditzy blonde preoccupied with boy drama  she embraced the role telling sidewalks  so i did end up getting the job which  totally changed the course truly of  actually my life and my career it kind  of put me on the map and made me realize  how much i love sitcoms when her  on-screen father john ritter died  suddenly in 2003 cuoco was heartbroken  and the show faced an unexpected  challenge new characters were introduced  and portrayed by actors trying to fill  ritter's role eight simple rules was  able to continue until 2005 but cuoco  would never forget the man so near and  dear to her heart to this day if anyone  asks me john ritter i i get this chill  because i love him  so much  in 2005 kaylee cuoco was offered a role  on the wb's charmed in its eighth season  she was initially nervous to come on as  billy jenkins a new witch among a  star-studded cast but she felt at home  after a warm welcome from alyssa milano  she told yahoo entertainment i know what  it's like when someone new comes on  there's people like alyssa who really do  mould your career and mould your path so  that was a really good moment cuoco  appeared in 22 episodes throughout the  final season and viewers hoped she might  get a spin-off series that was not to be  but fans would see her again on screen  soon enough  for one of her roles in the mid-2000s  kaylee was cast in the lifetime movie to  be fat like me in it she plays a high  school athlete who dons a fat suit in a  social experiment to see how differently  overweight people are treated by society  the film's reviews played out exactly as  you'd think they would for a lifetime  movie but cuoco's performance was  praised despite this film's blatantly  obvious message it's a decent showcase  of cuoco's skill as a dramatic actor of  course the biggest break in her career  saw her sticking to her comedy chops  when she first auditioned for the big  bang theory she didn't get the part of  penny in fact the role didn't even exist  early on cuoco tried out for a different  version of the character a girl named  katie but at 19 years old she was too  young for the part after filming the  first pilot producers decided to make  some changes that's when they created  penny brought cuoco back and cast her in  the role as she told entertainment  tonight i came in i got the job and it  got picked up and it was like this  whirlwind it was awesome penny started  off as a bubbly pretty girl next door  type but over the course of 12 seasons  on the show cuoco had the chance to put  her skills to work and ran with it she  created an edgier character with more  depth who played a major role in the  sitcom's success  kaylee's time on the big bang theory was  certainly a career highlight but it was  ultimately a stepping stone to her true  dream in 2012 kaylee organized a flash  mob featuring the casting crew on the  set of the big bang theory surprising  the audience and producers with a dance  routine with choreography helped by  kaylee's sister brianna after a video of  the flash mob went viral kaylee talked  about it at a paley center panel  it's just been a dream of mine  mom and i said guess what you're all  doing it with me  thankfully they got to do it again in  2014 and then once more during the  shooting of the final season  the success of the big bang theory soon  made kaylee cuoco a recognizable face in  the world of television comedy it wasn't  long until that face began appearing on  magazines in commercials and elsewhere  in hollywood cuoco also landed some  prestigious hosting gigs in 2011 she  hosted the teen choice awards as well as  the people's choice awards in 2012 and  2013. she wasn't just hosting award  shows either as she won emmys in 2014  and 2015. kaylee cuoco's tv stardom  doesn't end there she also made a splash  joining william shatner for a series of  priceline.com commercials cuoco played  shatner's character's daughter and she's  continued to promote priceline.com as  recently as 2022 she's also since done  tv spots for toyota and smirnoff vodka  the 2010 saw kaylee cuoco's career  expand beyond her beloved cbs sitcom in  2011 she spent her big bang hiatus  appearing alongside james marsden in the  easter themed family comedy hop the  movie found kaylee acting opposite a  computer animated character for the  first time but she also landed other  roles in much more adult comedies with  actual adults in 2014 she executive  produced and starred in authors  anonymous where she played a writer  whose overnight success results in the  ire of her former weekly writers group  she also played a supporting role in the  wedding ringer alongside kevin hart and  josh gad which received mostly negative  reviews from critics however she and gad  later reunited to compete against each  other in an episode of lip sync battle  in 2015 kaylee also starred in the  independent film burning bodhi about a  group of friends who reunite after one  of them passes away along with her  supporting role in 2011's the last ride  a biopic of country legend hank williams  this marked kaylie's first official  foray into dramatic film  the longer the big bang theory went on  the more its cast became sitcom royalty  it also became important that the show  didn't suffer a loss of actors which is  known to happen when sitcoms continue  for years this meant that over the  course of 12 seasons many of the show's  biggest stars received tremendous pay  raises in the first season the main trio  of cuoco johnny galecki and jim parsons  each earned 60 thousand dollars as their  salary for the entire season while the  other main cast members netted 45  thousand dollars cuoco and her cast  mates negotiated for higher payment in  2010 resulting in each actor gaining two  hundred thousand dollars per episode by  the last season cuoco galecki parsons  simon hellberg and kunal nayer were each  getting 1 million dollars per episode  making them one of the highest paid  casts in sitcom history post the big  bang theory cuoco's fortune has allowed  her to play a bigger role in executive  producing projects like harley quinn and  the flight attendant  in october 2017 kaylee cuoco founded her  own production company yes norman  productions entering a multi-year deal  with warner brothers to develop projects  together the first of these new  endeavors was an adaptation of the  crispo jallian novel the flight  attendant this limited series stars  cuoco as cassie bowden a flight  attendant who sleeps with the passenger  only to wake up to find his dead body in  bed with her the flight attendant  premiered on hbo max in november 2020  despite the show being originally  ordered as a limited series its success  led to hbo picking it up for a second  season which premiered in 2022 cuoco's  partnership with warner's continued in  2019 with the premiere of harley quinn  an adult animated series starring cuoco  as the titular villain  you're lucky i even showed up oh was  batman too busy doing this i'd  definitely make love two bats shut up  and battle me nars oh god  in summer 2018 variety reported that  series creator chuck laurie called the  cast into his office where jim parsons  announced the upcoming 12th season of  the big bang theory would be his last  sticking with lori's plan not to  continue without any of its main cast  members the show prepared to reach its  finale cuoco maybe more than the rest of  the cast was in shock at parson's  decision feeling as if she could have  continued on in may 2019 the cast and  crew gathered one last time in front of  a studio audience to shoot the series  finale in the final episode penny is  revealed to be pregnant which many fans  and critics felt was a betrayal of her  character arc what if what if we didn't  have kids  ever  i mean our life is so great why would we  want to change that unfortunately for  big bang fans hoping for a reunion  episode cuoco has no desire to have a  do-over on the series feeling satisfied  with how it ended in an interview on the  one show she claimed she'll never be  able to compare anything she does in the  future to her experience on the show  having a successful sitcom doesn't  guarantee success later in your career  as cuoco learned even after auditioning  for ryan johnson's sequel to knives out  she found out that she ultimately wasn't  cast in a cover story for glamour  magazine kaylee discussed how she was  convinced she had a part in the film but  the part instead went to kate hudson she  admitted that her bags were already  packed to head to greece where the movie  was shot but she didn't stay down for  long she was offered a role in meet cute  shortly after a romantic comedy she  ended up filming with pete davidson  [Music]

